Review of R14 · D2: no socket is opened during a normal novacore session
(author: antigravity, commit ba85896; board report ac0c6bf) by claude.
Date: 2026-10-17T02:30Z. HEAD: ac0c6bf. Host: Windows 11, Python 3.13.15.

Method. A byte-exact copy of HEAD's novacore/ and tools/ (`git -c
core.autocrlf=false archive HEAD novacore tools | tar -x -C <scratch>/rr3copy`).
Each break edits one source file in the copy, runs test_no_sockets.py, and
restores the bytes. A break that test_no_sockets.py does not catch is re-run
against the full novacore suite before it is called NOT CAUGHT. The planted
line is `import socket as _s; _s.socket().close()`: it raises no error, so
only the audit hook can see it. The script is in appendix A. The repository
was not edited.

=== 1. What the test does (read from novacore/tests/test_no_sockets.py)
  - Registers one audit hook at import; it records events whose name starts
    with "socket" only while a flag is set. The oracle is the interpreter.
  - With the flag set: load_config, MemoryStore, a Companion with
    FakeModelRunner, remember, search, one reply, CapabilityBroker status and
    two requests, UpdateProposalStore.create. Asserts zero events.
  - test_audit_hook_detects_socket_events_when_recording opens a real socket
    under the flag and asserts socket.__new__ is seen. This is the control.
  - The docstring states the limit: the external model runner is out of
    scope.

